{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And what the land, etc.</b> Meaning: corresponding to the specifics of what is made through others — namely, the structures of the city, the dwellings, and the vessels — whether it is good in glorious building, or bad in its buildings. Therefore he specified saying <b>that he dwells in it</b>. And corresponding to this particular you will find that the verse stated in parashat Va'etchanan (Deuteronomy 6:10–11): ״וְהָיָה כִּי יְבִיאֲךָ וְגוֹ׳ לָתֶת לָךְ עָרִים גְּדֹלוֹת וְטוֹבוֹת אֲשֶׁר לֹא בָנִיתָ״. And as part of the beauty of the city he mentioned also ״the camps, whether in fortresses,״ and our Sages of blessed memory interpreted (Numbers Rabbah 16) that he gave them a sign — and this is the way of derash. But the plain sense of the verse is that the main thrust of the entire inquiry is only about the land; but as for the people, it is plain that they are a great and tall people, sons of Anak, giants, and there is no doubt about this to spy them out. And when we say that he alluded to them also about the might of the men, the intention would be to tell them to observe the extent of their strength, in order to recognize the wonders of El who shields them by their hand."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:23.337825450Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}